  "why_it_fell": {
    "value": "Down 35% from its May 2026 high on handset weakness (handset revenue -20% y/y on OEM inventory drawdown and memory cost inflation), Apple's accelerating in-house modem transition (QCOM iPhone modem share falling from ~20% toward zero by 2027), and a cut to Q4 FY26 guidance below consensus on both revenue and EPS at the Jul 29 print.",
    "source": "https://www.foreignpolicyjournal.com/2026/08/28/qualcomm-nasdaq-qcom-stock-price-slides-31-as-costs-hit-now-and-non-handset-growth-remains-years-away/",
    "as_of": "2026-08-28"
  },
  "judgment": {
    "prospect_pts": 4,
    "prospect_why": "The case is that automotive and IoT and a data-centre win offset the loss of the Apple modem, and it depends on the $6B auto exit-rate; the offset is guided but the loss is contractual and dated to roughly zero share by 2027, so the negative is more certain than the positive.",
    "competition_pts": 3,
    "competition_why": "Gross margin narrowed from 55.3% to 53.1% over four quarters while its largest customer designs it out, which is the losing-share pattern; the offset is that at 16.6x forward it is cheaper than AVGO at 18.6x and MRVL at 33.0x.",
    "macro_fit_pts": 6,
    "macro_fit_why": "This is the regime's preferred shape: $9,979M of TTM free cash flow at 16.6x forward earnings gives a visible cash-flow yield that clears the 5.37% single-A hurdle, and value led all factors over one and three months.",
    "narrative_pts": 4,
    "narrative_why": "It is a semiconductor company the market does not count as an AI winner but as a handset company being disintermediated, so it sits outside the accelerating themes and moves on its own numbers."
  }
